  "problem": "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ compute $P(-2.20<Z<2.10).$\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-2.2\\,$ | $\\,0.0139\\,$ | $\\,0.0143\\,$ | $\\,0.0146\\,$ |\n| $\\,-2.1\\,$ | $\\,0.0179\\,$ | $\\,0.0183\\,$ | $\\,0.0188\\,$ |\n| $\\,-2.0\\,$ | $\\,0.0228\\,$ | $\\,0.0232\\,$ | $\\,0.0239\\,$ |\n\n$P(-2.20<Z<2.10)=$\n{{field-1}}",
